    {
      "id": "67d966033bbe22f0d50c7c6d",
      "endpoint": "DynamicMetadata",
      "description": "Save metadata into Nuxeo.",
      "model": "anthropic.claude-3-sonnet-20240229-v1:0",
      "prompt": "I am providing you with the Schema definition for the asset that needs to enriched. Schema is provided in JSON format.\n\nEach field contains the following properties:\n\n- description\n- type\n\nOptionally a field may include a list of valid values found in the property:\n\n - dictionaryValues\n\nThe possible values in the dictionary included as a comma seperated list as ID followed by the value.\n\nHere is an example schema to be populated:\n\n{\n\"nxtag:tags\":{\"description\":\"A list of tags describing the asset to aid in searching and cacegorization\",\"type\":\"array\"},\n\"dc:nature\":{\"description\":\"A category of type of asset\",\"dictionaryValues\":{\"note\":\"papernote\",\"email\":\"electronic message\"},\"type\":\"string\"}\n}\n\nOur goal is to generate the populated schema. Here is an example of the above schema populated:\n\"nxtag:tags\":[\"communication\", \"notes\", \"message\"]\n\"dc:nature\": \"note\"\n\nIMPORTANT RULES:\n\n- Extract metadata from the attached image\n- Format the response as a JSON object as described above with the extracted metadata.\n- If a property called directoryValues exists in the schema for a field you MUST ensure the extracted value matches one of the provided values in the directoryvalues.\n- If there is not a value that matches in the filed type \"directory\", do not provide a value\n \nYou are an AI specialized in extracting metadata from Nuxeo documents. Given a document and its associated schema generate a structured JSON output where:\n\nEach key corresponds to the Nuxeo XPath schema field.\n\nThe extracted metadata is accurate. If you can't identify a proper value for a field, please return null for that field.\nThe JSON output is well-structured and properly formatted.\nReturn the JSON response as valid code object syntax without irrelevant text or characthers like: json \n\nYou must call the \"metadata_extractor\" tool to return your answer.\nExtract metadata from the document and populate the tool input according to the schema.\nDo not answer in plain text — only call the tool.\n                                \nPopulate ALL required fields in the tool's input JSON using the document provided.\nIf a value is unknown, return null for that field, not an empty object.",
